    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d893">

                <pb facs="0881" n="769" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg769"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5100a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Commission to Negotiate
                        Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-20T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 20,
                                1919—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2886. For Polk.</p>
                <p>Vice Consul Burri at headquarters of General Denikine in Ekaterinodar in recent
                    report refers to officers of American Military Mission in his district. Are such
                    officers operating with General Denikine or elsewhere in South Russia? and if so
                    Department would be glad to know conditions which they report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
